Kim: Okay, awesome.

20
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:19.939
Kim: So, as part of the Ubuntu 2204 upgrade, what I'm doing is I'm moving forward to a Docker implementation only.

21
00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:27.540
Kim: And what this looks like is…

22
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:42.120
Kim: Indy Plenum produces Docker images, and then IndyNode will produce Docker images based off of Indy Plenum's images. This simplifies the release workflow.

23
00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:51.940
Kim: Instead of creating Debian packages, there's a lot of overhead getting the Debian packages working correctly, and the tooling seems to be falling out of support.

24
00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:57.040
Kim: And so this should simplify our deployment methodology.

25
00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.160
Kim: What I'm showing here…

26
00:04:59.970 --> 00:05:14.620
Kim: is, in my local environment, I've got the, the build working. It creates a base image, and then the production image for Indy Plenum, and then it runs through the tests, and we can see that all the tests are passing.

27
00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:23.520
Kim: And then this will move over into… The IndyNode environment.

28
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:34.819
Kim: I actually don't remember where I left off on this. I think it's still work in progress. I think I'm working on getting the actions triggered right now.

29
00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:47.359
Kim: And then hopefully we'll have an IndyNode and Indy Platinum build based off of Ubuntu in a Docker container, and then we'll move on to the testing phase.

30
00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:53.230
Kim: Any questions, Lynn?

31
00:05:55.090 --> 00:06:05.990
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Yeah, so… I think you said last time that the… the upgrade from 20.04 to 2204 is gonna have to be…

32
00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.120
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): manual this time. It sounds like the reason is because we have to switch to Docker containers.

33
00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.630
Kim: Exactly.

34
00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:28.279
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): And so what about future upgrades? Well, we… there's a… there's a feature in Indy where you can trigger an upgrade from a remote location, and it will automatically update itself. Will that…

35
00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:33.339
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): be able to happen in the future? Will all upgrades from here on out have to be manual?

36
00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:38.080
Kim: I'm trying to, make it so that…

37
00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.909
Kim: We can send a signal

38
00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:45.439
Kim: to the Docker container to stop processing.

39
00:06:45.650 --> 00:06:47.050
Kim: To, to exit?

40
00:06:47.400 --> 00:07:02.539
Kim: And then if your Docker image is configured to be off of the latest image, on restart Kubernetes or Docker, I'm hoping that it will gather the latest image.

41
00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:13.610
Kim: based on the repository that you're configured to access, and that would be the upgrade mechanism for the Docker environment.

42
00:07:14.020 --> 00:07:18.489
Kim: Is to trigger a, a stop.

43
00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:25.999
Kim: And then, rely on Kubernetes or Docker to fetch the latest image on startup.

44
00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:37.759
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Okay, so… Hopefully, latest image is a…

45
00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:42.439
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): is configurable as well, so you can get whatever image you want, I guess, for…

46
00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.489
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): So that your whole, your whole,

47
00:07:46.550 --> 00:07:50.719
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Make sure your whole network is in agreement with whatever image.

48
00:07:50.720 --> 00:08:00.029
Kim: Yeah, so likely for your network, you would want to set up a Docker repository, and then have whatever image you want deployed labeled as latest.

49
00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:03.999
Kim: In that Docker repository.

50
00:08:05.550 --> 00:08:09.649
Kim: Then that would give you the control to determine

51
00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:14.249
Kim: What image is being deployed on your, in your environment?

52
00:08:18.650 --> 00:08:26.550
Kim: There still needs to be some testing done on that process to ensure that we have a reliable way to manage that.

53
00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:29.839
Kim: But that's the direction I'm looking at.

54
00:08:31.920 --> 00:08:32.740
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Okay.

55
00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:44.130
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Sounds like it's gonna be a several-month upgrade when we finally get to upgrading the… the networks.

56
