59
00:09:07.090 --> 00:09:11.450
Kim: So that we don't have to go through a several-month-long process.

60
00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:19.350
Kim: Let me just point the Docker Compose configuration to use the same data storage path.

61
00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.360
Kim: As the previous install.

62
00:09:24.010 --> 00:09:30.650
Kim: But it would still require, a manual process on each of the servers.

63
00:09:43.080 --> 00:09:50.659
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Yeah, that's the part that's the hard part, is the manual part, where we have to coordinate all the different node operators, and…

64
00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:56.340
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): And, helped them to get through the… I think.

65
00:09:56.340 --> 00:10:03.080
Kim: I think there would be a manual process… oh, there's gonna be a manual process regardless, because you're upgrading your OS level, too.

66
00:10:05.560 --> 00:10:08.380
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Well, there's… there's scripts that can run that will…

67
00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:19.209
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): That will make it so the OS doesn't require an upgrade, but it… we're not doing that anyway, so it doesn't matter. But there's… I think there's scripts that'll upgrade from 20 to 22.

68
00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:21.680
Lynn Bendixsen (Indicio): Without.

69
00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:29.450
